1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Playing Games

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:05,900
Oh, Daddy!

3
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,400
We had such a good time at the aquarium.

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,400
I saw a real shark.

5
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,550
I could almost touch it.

6
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:12,420
I'm so glad.

7
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:13,740
Hi. Michelle,

8
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:15,610
why don't you introduce everybody to Susan?

9
00:00:15,610 --> 00:00:16,200
Hi, Susan.

10
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,900
Hi.

11
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,300
I'd like you to meet Audrey and her mother, Mrs. Cooper.

12
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:21,590
Hello, Audrey.

13
00:00:21,590 --> 00:00:23,200
Nice to meet you, Mrs. Cooper.

14
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,700
I'm Susan Stewart.

15
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:27,300
And this is Shirley and Nicole.

16
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,550
Hi, girls.

17
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:29,060
Come on in.

18
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:29,600
Come on in, Mrs. Cooper.

19
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:30,600
Come on in, everybody.

20
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,100
The aquarium was so exciting.

21
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,600
I had never been there before.

22
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,500
The girls learned a great deal.

23
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:36,100
Frankly, so did I.

24
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,800
Well, please sit down

25
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:40,080
and tell us all about it during lunch.

26
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:42,070
We prepared some tuna fish

27
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:44,800
and cheese sandwiches for lunch.

28
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,290
I love tuna fish.

29
00:00:46,290 --> 00:00:50,400
Don't you, Audrey?

30
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,500
I remember when I used to be a Girl Scout.

31
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,500
My mother would take us everywhere, too.

32
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:58,000
Susan, I understand you're in the toy business.

33
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,300
Yes, I am.

34
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:01,000
My company manufactures toys and games for children.

35
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,800
Susan's vice-president in charge of new toys and games.

36
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,700
And the marketing of new toys and games.

37
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,500
Can we test a new game for you, Susan?

38
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,530
That's an excellent idea, Michelle.

39
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:12,300
I happen to have

40
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:13,000
a game which I brought home to study.

41
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,200
Let us try it!

42
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,300
Do you want to play?

43
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:20,000
Nicole? Shirley? Audrey?

44
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,010
We tested it last week on twelve- to fifteen-year-olds,

45
00:01:23,010 --> 00:01:25,700
and they found it to be too easy--

46
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:28,100
in other words ... boring.

47
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:31,000
We think it might be just right for ten- to twelve-year-olds.

48
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,400
That's us, Susan.

49
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:35,900
First, you shuffle the deck

50
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:39,200
and lay them face down.

51
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,940
Then you select the leader.

52
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:44,700
I'll be the leader.

53
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,220
The leader takes the first ten cards

54
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:50,380
and lays them face up on this stand.

55
00:01:50,380 --> 00:02:12,700
h-t-e-r-c-z-e-p-e-s.

56
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:15,290
Everyone gets a turn, going counterclockwise,

57
00:02:15,290 --> 00:02:16,800
left to right.

58
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:23,020
You have thirty seconds to make a word,

59
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:25,400
using as many letters as possible.

60
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:28,300
You get one point for each letter,

61
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:33,500
plus the person with the longest word gets ten extra points.

62
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:35,900
The first one to get one hundred points wins.

63
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:37,600
That's easy.

64
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,100
OK, let's go around the table.

65
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:48,900
You first, Audrey.

66
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:56,000
Chest--c-h-e-s-t.

67
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,600
Good.

68
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:00,300
That's five points.

69
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:07,400
Next, Nicole.

70
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:14,900
Three--t-h-r-e-e.

71
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:15,600
OK.

72
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,600
That's five points also.

73
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:25,100
It's your turn, Shirley.

74
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:32,500
Creep--c-r-e-e-p.

75
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,100
Creep.

76
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:36,300
That's another five-letter word.

77
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:36,600
Five points.

78
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,600
So far, you're all tied.

79
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:41,300
Sheet--s-h-e-e-t.

80
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:45,600
Sheet is a five-letter word.

81
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,900
Michelle, your turn.

82
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:51,900
Cheese--c-h-e-e-s-e.

83
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:52,520
Terrific!

84
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,600
Michelle wins with a six-letter word,

85
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,100
plus she gets an additional ten points

86
00:03:57,100 --> 00:03:59,270
for a total of sixteen points.

87
00:03:59,270 --> 00:04:01,100
How are you enjoying the game so far?

88
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:03,500
I think it's too easy.

89
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:04,900
Too easy?

90
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,100
Michelle!

91
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:07,700
It's OK, Harry.

92
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:08,800
Michelle is quite right.

93
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,800
She just said it's too easy.

94
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,640
Well, I like the game.

95
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,400
I enjoyed lunch, Susan.

96
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,100
Thank you so much,

97
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:17,900
but we have to get going

98
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:20,400
to meet the rest of the troop at two o'clock at the museum.

99
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:23,040
Oh, it was nice meeting all of you.

100
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,620
I hope you have a wonderful time

101
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:26,200
at the Museum of Natural History.

102
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,100
Good-bye, everybody.

103
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,080
Have a good time.

104
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:29,030
Bye.

105
00:04:29,030 --> 00:04:29,830
See you in front of the museum at five o'clock.

106
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:31,800
Oh, OK.

107
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:32,660
Thanks, Mr. Bennett.

108
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:33,780
That'll be fine.

109
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:37,300
And thanks again for the lunch and for the game.

110
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,400
Good-bye, Susan.

111
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,760
It's not a bad game.

112
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:43,900
It's just ... slow.

113
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,400
Just slow.

114
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,900
You helped save our company a lot of money.

115
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:59,200
Bye-bye.

116
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:03,900
You are wonderful with kids.

117
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,900
I am.

118
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:08,900
Isn't there a conversation that we have to finish?
